# CLISP's compiled translation units -- SHARED by mkfile.rebuild and
# mkfile.runtime, and shared rather than copied on purpose.
#
# `mkfile.rebuild' turns `*.d' into `*.c'; `mkfile.runtime' compiles a
# SUBSET of those `.c' and links them.  The subset is the point:
# CLISP's build has 132 `.d' files and only the names below become
# objects -- everything else (`lispbibl', every `spvw_*', every
# `arilev*') is `#include'd INTO one of these, which is why the build
# directory is full of `.c' files nothing compiles.
#
# **Two copies of this list would drift**, and the failure mode is not
# a missing file: a name dropped from the runtime's copy is a
# translation unit that is generated, never compiled, and shows up as
# undefined symbols at the LINK with nothing nearby to say why.  *This
# tree has paid for a hand-maintained list falling out of step with the
# thing it describes four times* -- perl's `config.h' against its
# `Config.pm', bash's `config.h', the six `SIZEOF_*' files -- so the
# list lives in one file and both mkfiles read it with `<'.
#
# Adapted from `makemake.in'.  This port disables dynamic FFI, threads
# and optional modules, which is why no `*_mod' name appears.

CPARTS=\
	spvw spvwtabf spvwtabs spvwtabo\
	eval control encoding pathname stream socket io funarg\
	array hashtabl list package record weak sequence charstrg debug\
	error misc time predtype symbol lisparit i18n unixaux built

# gnulib, and it is FOUR FILES rather than eleven.
#
# `gllib/Makefile.am' distinguishes `libgnu_a_SOURCES' (always built)
# from `EXTRA_libgnu_a_SOURCES' (built only when the system lacks the
# function).  **All eight of the EXTRA ones are in libap already** --
# `alloca', `getpagesize', `gettimeofday', `mbrtowc', `mbsinit',
# `mbsrtowcs', `memchr', `nl_langinfo' -- measured with
# `sys/lib/tests/apfunc-sweep.py' rather than assumed, each reported
# `defined' with the implementing file named.  What is left is the two
# that are gnulib's own rather than libc's, plus the two Unicode
# tables, which no libc has.
#
# *Adding one of the eight back would not be harmless*: it would give
# the link two definitions of a libc function, which is the `f2c'
# `redefinition: malloc' shape this tree already records.
GLPARTS=\
	localcharset strnlen1 uniname/uniname uniwidth/width
